{
  "_comment": [
    "Catalog corpus. Each case is one catalog document.",
    "valid=true: load succeeds; `messages` is the expected flat result keyed by dotted path: {msg} or {msg, desc}. `msg` is the MessageFormat 2 source exactly as written (a port parses it with its MF2 library; the parse tree is not pinned here).",
    "valid=false: load fails with exactly `code` at dotted message `key` (\"\" = whole document). Only the first error in document order is pinned; each invalid case contains exactly one fault.",
    "`doc` is the catalog as JSON; `raw` replaces it when the fault is in the bytes (invalid JSON, duplicate object key, trailing data). schema_gap: the fault is not expressible in catalog.schema.json, so the schema accepts the document. `invalid_message` cases are all schema_gap: the schema does not parse MF2.",
    "Every message in a valid case MUST parse as MessageFormat 2 with no syntax or data-model error; `unknown-function-loads` shows that an unregistered function is a formatting-time error, not a load error.",
    "All text is fake."
  ],
